              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners (Joel D. Bertocchi), petitioners rely on sections 251 and 252 of the Telecommunications Act, which impose interconnection duties on incumbent carriers and set procedures for negotiating those duties."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners (Mr. Bertocchi)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "d5a4950198d9dfe4bc27b4b1df24696f23ea57b60a95ddaec5f7cedb5a0692c0",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-d5a4950198d9-0003-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 53,
                "start": 53
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners (Mr. Bertocchi), petitioners argue that Ex parte Young does not apply because the statute does not permit suing state commissioners in federal court; e(6) does not reference state commissioners."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners (Mr. Bertocchi)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "d5a4950198d9dfe4bc27b4b1df24696f23ea57b60a95ddaec5f7cedb5a0692c0",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-d5a4950198d9-0003-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 54,
                "start": 54
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners (Mr. Bertocchi), petitioners describe the Illinois Commerce Commission proceeding as a quasi\u2011judicial proceeding, not a legislative or executive action."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners (Mr. Bertocchi)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "d5a4950198d9dfe4bc27b4b1df24696f23ea57b60a95ddaec5f7cedb5a0692c0",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-d5a4950198d9-0003-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 55,
                "start": 55
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners (Mr. Bertocchi), petitioners contend that the contract at issue violates the Telecommunications Act and that jurisdiction cannot be limited to violations of federal law alone."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioners",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Paul M. Smith",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "d5a4950198d9dfe4bc27b4b1df24696f23ea57b60a95ddaec5f7cedb5a0692c0",
